# One ignore file, for the whole repository.
#
# Nothing in the toolchain reads .gitignore, so splitting it per directory buys
# no isolation. Wrangler uploads whatever is in edge/public/ regardless of what
# Git thinks -- the live site serves texmf/swiftlatexpdftex.fmt, which Git does
# not track. There is no submodule and no nested repository here either. What a
# split does cost is the same rule written in two places, free to disagree.
#
# It matters most for the *.json section below. That is a deny-by-default
# security rule with named exceptions, and a second ignore file that cannot see
# it is exactly how one of those exceptions gets silently killed.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ secrets

# Environment variables.
#
# .env carried the Gemini key for the Python application that used to live
# here. The edge Worker takes its secrets from `wrangler secret put` and, for
# local development, from edge/.dev.vars. The wildcards cover the variants
# someone might create later -- wrangler also reads .dev.vars.<environment>,
# and a .dev.vars.production that was not ignored would be a committed
# credential.
.env
.env.*
*.env
edge/.dev.vars*

# Credentials and keys.
#
# Deny-by-default: every .json is ignored, and the few that are genuinely safe
# to publish are named below. The Firebase Admin SDK service-account key is a
# .json and grants full administrative access to the project, so the blanket
# rule is the point of this section - do not replace it with a named pattern.
*.json
# Firebase project configuration - identifies the project, holds no secret.
!firebase.json
!firestore.indexes.json
!database.rules.json
# Node manifests. The lockfiles are committed so `npm ci` reproduces the exact
# trees the suites were verified against.
!package.json
!package-lock.json
# Frozen test data. The parity references were produced by the Python
# implementation that is no longer in this repository, and the bench manifests
# describe fixture images that are no longer generated -- so both are source
# now, not output. Neither holds a secret.
!edge/tests/reference/*.json
!bench/manifest_*.json
# The formula recogniser's vocabulary. It sits beside the two .onnx files in
# edge/model-src/mfr-int8/ and is as much a part of that model as they are --
# without it `npm run build:models` cannot rebuild public/models/mfr. The
# deny-by-default rule above was hiding it.
!edge/model-src/mfr-int8/tokenizer.json

# Certificates and private keys in any other form.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
*.der

# ------------------------------------------------------------- build output

# The runtime asset trees Cloudflare serves. Three are build output and are
# ignored: build-models.mjs takes ORT and Tesseract from the packages the
# lockfile pins and copies the committed edge/model-src/mfr-int8/ weights, and
# each result is byte-identical to what is deployed.
#
# Two are NOT ignored, on purpose. edge/public/texmf/ (the TeX Live subset and
# the SwiftLaTeX format file) and edge/public/models/tessdata/ (the language
# data) have no source in this repository -- one was harvested from a TeX Live
# installation, the other copied from an installed Tesseract -- so they are
# committed as the frozen artefacts they are. That is what lets a clean clone
# rebuild the whole of public/ and deploy it. Not Git LFS: a checkout that
# skips the LFS smudge (actions/checkout by default, or any machine without
# git-lfs) leaves 133-byte pointer files that EXIST, so check:assets passes
# and wrangler publishes the pointers over the live site.
#
# The recogniser weights are the INPUT to build-models, which is why they live
# in edge/model-src/ and not in a directory called build/: they are tracked,
# and a blanket `build/` rule here would silently untrack 31 MB of source.
edge/public/models/mfr/
edge/public/vendor/ort/
edge/public/vendor/tesseract/

# Test output: screenshots, probe scripts, built PDFs.
edge/tests/out/

# Benchmark leftovers. img_mixed/, img_pages/, img_math/ and the manifests
# beside them are frozen fixtures the edge suite reads, and they are committed
# for that reason -- see bench/README.md. These four are what the generators
# that no longer exist used to produce, and nothing reads them.
bench/img/
bench/img_hard/
bench/img_deskewed/
bench/results_*.json

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- local

# Node. Matches at any depth, so edge/node_modules/ is covered too.
node_modules/

# Cloudflare/Wrangler local state.
edge/.wrangler/

# Firebase CLI local state: emulator data, deploy caches and debug logs.
.firebase/
*.log

# Python. Only edge/tools/build-mfr.py remains, and it is run by hand to
# rebuild the formula recogniser's weights.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
